(4830057, 695270, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Color, Saturation, and Hue:  Colors are beautiful, very realstic.  Nothing looks over saturated or over processed.<br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast:  Both are excellent.  Highlights are not blown out, contrast is appropriate for this image, shadows hold details very well.  Over all lighting is very good.  Nice work...<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  Focus is excellent.  Extremely sharp, as it should be in this case.  Depth of field works well.<br/> <br/>I might have liked a little tighter crop to get a better look at the birds.  I like the separation of the one, from the other two.  I might have like the two on the right a bit closer, but then this isn''t like posing people.  Perhaps one bird facing the camera would have been a bit better also, but then again, it isn''t like they take direction.<br/> <br/>Beautiful birds, and I really enjoyed this photograph.  Congratulations on a well deserved top ten finish.  You were up against some really good stuff.  In another challenge, you might well have taken home a ribbon.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club Review: Color, Saturation, and Hue:  Colors are beautiful, very realstic.  Nothing looks over saturated or over processed. Brightness and Contrast:  Both are excellent.  Highlights are not blown out, contrast is appropriate for this image, shadows hold details very well.  Over all lighting is very good.  Nice work... Focus and depth of field:  Focus is excellent.  Extremely sharp, as it should be in this case.  Depth of field works well. I might have liked a little tighter crop to get a better look at the birds.  I like the separation of the one, from the other two.  I might have like the two on the right a bit closer, but then this isn''t like posing people.  Perhaps one bird facing the camera would have been a bit better also, but then again, it isn''t like they take direction. Beautiful birds, and I really enjoyed this photograph.  Congratulations on a well deserved top ten finish.  You were up against some really good stuff.  In another challenge, you might well have taken home a ribbon. ', '2008-07-16 23:18:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4830505, 695270, 89341, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=697253" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697253.gif'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697253.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697253.gif"/></a> from me in <a href="//dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=797556" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Posthumous Ribbons</a> <br/> <br/>This was my fav shot in the challenge and my only 10. I loved the colour and the reflections and the fact all the birds were doing something different. I also really like the water through the whole background with nothing else to disturb it</td>', ' from me in Posthumous Ribbons  This was my fav shot in the challenge and my only 10. I loved the colour and the reflections and the fact all the birds were doing something different. I also really like the water through the whole background with nothing else to disturb it', '2008-07-17 05:25:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4830509, 695359, 89341, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=697251" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697251.gif'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697251.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697251.gif"/></a> from me in <a href="//dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=797556" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Posthumous Ribbons</a> <br/> <br/>Lovely shot and great focus and exposure, the reflection is a huge bonus too</td>', ' from me in Posthumous Ribbons  Lovely shot and great focus and exposure, the reflection is a huge bonus too', '2008-07-17 05:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4830513, 695839, 89341, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=697252" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697252.gif'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697252.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697252.gif"/></a> from me in <a href="//dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=797556" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Posthumous Ribbons</a> <br/> <br/>The clarity of this shot is awesome, the reflection and the surface and background all work well for me</td>', ' from me in Posthumous Ribbons  The clarity of this shot is awesome, the reflection and the surface and background all work well for me', '2008-07-17 05:27:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4830557, 695270, 91131, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bobonacus:</b></div><hr/><i> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=697253" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697253.gif'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697253.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89341/120/697253.gif"/></a> from me in <a href="//dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=797556" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Posthumous Ribbons</a> <br/> <br/>This was my fav shot in the challenge and my only 10. I loved the colour and the reflections and the fact all the birds were doing something different. I also really like the water through the whole background with nothing else to disturb it </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wow a 10?! I am truly honored and appreciate so much the PH ribbon. The public forum was a big step for me - still learning how to navigate. The grace and kindness of DPC folks is inspiring. You have made my week!</td>', 'Originally posted by bobonacus:  from me in Posthumous Ribbons  This was my fav shot in the challenge and my only 10. I loved the colour and the reflections and the fact all the birds were doing something different. I also really like the water through the whole background with nothing else to disturb it   Wow a 10?! I am truly honored and appreciate so much the PH ribbon. The public forum was a big step for me - still learning how to navigate. The grace and kindness of DPC folks is inspiring. You have made my week!', '2008-07-17 06:28:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4830568, 695270, 91131, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ambaker:</b></div><hr/><i> Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Color, Saturation, and Hue:  Colors are beautiful, very realstic.  Nothing looks over saturated or over processed.<br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast:  Both are excellent.  Highlights are not blown out, contrast is appropriate for this image, shadows hold details very well.  Over all lighting is very good.  Nice work...<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  Focus is excellent.  Extremely sharp, as it should be in this case.  Depth of field works well.<br/> <br/>I might have liked a little tighter crop to get a better look at the birds.  I like the separation of the one, from the other two.  I might have like the two on the right a bit closer, but then this isn''t like posing people.  Perhaps one bird facing the camera would have been a bit better also, but then again, it isn''t like they take direction.<br/> <br/>Beautiful birds, and I really enjoyed this photograph.  Congratulations on a well deserved top ten finish.  You were up against some really good stuff.  In another challenge, you might well have taken home a ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Grateful for your evaluation and kind encouragement. Wildlife is challenging and DPC has provided an opportunity to learn. Not only that but to appreciate and enjoy the incredible talent and creativity displayed by many. Some are truly gifted. Thanks again.</td>', 'Originally posted by ambaker: Critique Club Review: Color, Saturation, and Hue:  Colors are beautiful, very realstic.  Nothing looks over saturated or over processed. Brightness and Contrast:  Both are excellent.  Highlights are not blown out, contrast is appropriate for this image, shadows hold details very well.  Over all lighting is very good.  Nice work... Focus and depth of field:  Focus is excellent.  Extremely sharp, as it should be in this case.  Depth of field works well. I might have liked a little tighter crop to get a better look at the birds.  I like the separation of the one, from the other two.  I might have like the two on the right a bit closer, but then this isn''t like posing people.  Perhaps one bird facing the camera would have been a bit better also, but then again, it isn''t like they take direction. Beautiful birds, and I really enjoyed this photograph.  Congratulations on a well deserved top ten finish.  You were up against some really good stuff.  In another challenge, you might well have taken home a ribbon.   Grateful for your evaluation and kind encouragement. Wildlife is challenging and DPC has provided an opportunity to learn. Not only that but to appreciate and enjoy the incredible talent and creativity displayed by many. Some are truly gifted. Thanks again.', '2008-07-17 06:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4831130, 695270, 35892, '<td valign="top">this is a wonderful image!</td>', 'this is a wonderful image!', '2008-07-17 16:18:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4831134, 696060, 78064, '<td valign="top">Hi Sue!!  Wow, fantastic job!!  I love it!  Soon I will be getting a new camera as well....I will be calling you!  P.S.  The sunflowers are really getting big.......</td>', 'Hi Sue!!  Wow, fantastic job!!  I love it!  Soon I will be getting a new camera as well....I will be calling you!  P.S.  The sunflowers are really getting big.......', '2008-07-17 16:20:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4831431, 695825, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Jane,<br/> <br/>       Nice image. Your composition/Framing is dead on and your exposure is really well done. The colors are nice and rich and I really like the way you captured the sutle greens. The image is nice and clean, tac sharp and the details are wonderful. The texture in the feathers is really nice also. The image has plenty of interest &amp; held my attention completely. The title fits the challenge imo, overall this is a really nice image that is really well done.</td>', 'Hi Jane,        Nice image. Your composition/Framing is dead on and your exposure is really well done. The colors are nice and rich and I really like the way you captured the sutle greens. The image is nice and clean, tac sharp and the details are wonderful. The texture in the feathers is really nice also. The image has plenty of interest & held my attention completely. The title fits the challenge imo, overall this is a really nice image that is really well done.', '2008-07-17 18:29:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4831467, 695378, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Glenn,<br/> <br/>        Nice image, it is simple yet very effective. The image for me has lots of interest. The color scheme is well done as is the composition/framing. Your exposure is dead on and the details in the rose are excellent. The image is clean &amp; sharp, &amp; I like the frontal bok makes the image more interesting imo. Your title fits the challenge very well also. One credit is do, that of the assistant for a job well done :).</td>', 'Hi Glenn,         Nice image, it is simple yet very effective. The image for me has lots of interest. The color scheme is well done as is the composition/framing. Your exposure is dead on and the details in the rose are excellent. The image is clean & sharp, & I like the frontal bok makes the image more interesting imo. Your title fits the challenge very well also. One credit is do, that of the assistant for a job well done :).', '2008-07-17 18:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4831702, 695398, 55838, '<td valign="top">Such a beautiful shot - I''m suprized it didn''t score north of 6.</td>', 'Such a beautiful shot - I''m suprized it didn''t score north of 6.', '2008-07-17 22:17:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4831715, 695381, 10818, '<td valign="top">What an awesome old car, and a great photo.</td>', 'What an awesome old car, and a great photo.', '2008-07-17 22:22:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4831835, 694786, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Color, Saturation, and Hue:  Colors are obviously manipulated for effect, but work well for this composition.<br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast:  Both are very good.  Plenty of great detail is visible, with nothing overly bright or overly dark.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  Focus is very sharp, depth of field is appropriate for this image.<br/> <br/>This image is quite interesting.  The background is very busy, and it competes with the leaf like crazy.  At the same time, the color manipulation makes things look a bit out of focus, unless you look close.  Centering the subject is the kiss of death to the rule of thirds purists, and likely hurt your score quite a bit.  <br/> <br/>I think the biggest problem is that this is the wrong medium for this image.  The presentation on the computer screen for voting isn''t large enough to do this image justice.  As I sat here looking at this and trying to figure out what was really grabbing me, and what I wanted out of it, I realized I want to see this image BIG!  You''ve moved the leaf from straight photograph to art.  I could see this blown up on a wall in a bank lobby or a gallery.  If this image was about five feet tall, I think it would really come into its own.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Color, Saturation, and Hue:  Colors are obviously manipulated for effect, but work well for this composition. Brightness and Contrast:  Both are very good.  Plenty of great detail is visible, with nothing overly bright or overly dark. Focus and depth of field:  Focus is very sharp, depth of field is appropriate for this image. This image is quite interesting.  The background is very busy, and it competes with the leaf like crazy.  At the same time, the color manipulation makes things look a bit out of focus, unless you look close.  Centering the subject is the kiss of death to the rule of thirds purists, and likely hurt your score quite a bit.   I think the biggest problem is that this is the wrong medium for this image.  The presentation on the computer screen for voting isn''t large enough to do this image justice.  As I sat here looking at this and trying to figure out what was really grabbing me, and what I wanted out of it, I realized I want to see this image BIG!  You''ve moved the leaf from straight photograph to art.  I could see this blown up on a wall in a bank lobby or a gallery.  If this image was about five feet tall, I think it would really come into its own.', '2008-07-18 00:01:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4831868, 694786, 48228, '<td valign="top">I like the textures and bold color in this one..... For the ''Point of Color'' challenge, it may be just a tad to busy, but I still like it very much.....</td>', 'I like the textures and bold color in this one..... For the ''Point of Color'' challenge, it may be just a tad to busy, but I still like it very much.....', '2008-07-18 00:17:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832312, 696060, 74911, '<td valign="top">Big congrats on your ribbon. I knew this would ribbon. Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>I don''t understand how somebody can give a 2 for this kinda shot.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-18 10:52:35.</i></td>', 'Big congrats on your ribbon. I knew this would ribbon. Keep up the good work. I don''t understand how somebody can give a 2 for this kinda shot.', '2008-07-18 11:50:39.000000', '2008-07-18 11:52:35.000000', 0),
(4832479, 696122, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Nathan,<br/> <br/>        Nice image, The detail in the eye is outstanding. The one thing here is the reflection in the eye, it kept catching mine &amp; I found myself trying to figure out if it was a window or a mirror. The background (purple) tho pleasent was also a bit of a distraction. Getting back to the eye, the deep rich blue color is fantastic. I had a bit of trouble with the crop as a portraiture per-say but thought it is an excellent abstract-portraiture and it fit nicely. I love your use of dof here, it is outstanding as is the exposure. Overall I like the image it is interesting, clean, well composted and sharp as a tac.</td>', 'Hi Nathan,         Nice image, The detail in the eye is outstanding. The one thing here is the reflection in the eye, it kept catching mine & I found myself trying to figure out if it was a window or a mirror. The background (purple) tho pleasent was also a bit of a distraction. Getting back to the eye, the deep rich blue color is fantastic. I had a bit of trouble with the crop as a portraiture per-say but thought it is an excellent abstract-portraiture and it fit nicely. I love your use of dof here, it is outstanding as is the exposure. Overall I like the image it is interesting, clean, well composted and sharp as a tac.', '2008-07-18 13:59:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832540, 694924, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Steve,<br/> <br/>        Great image, I really like it. The composition is really well done the angle is perfect. The chest it is laying on is a really nice accent and fits really well. The color scheme of the overall image really works well here. You did a really nice job keeping the texture in the cap also. The image is simple yet extremely effective, it is clean, sharp with vivid, deep, rich color. Should have scored higher imo.</td>', 'Hi Steve,         Great image, I really like it. The composition is really well done the angle is perfect. The chest it is laying on is a really nice accent and fits really well. The color scheme of the overall image really works well here. You did a really nice job keeping the texture in the cap also. The image is simple yet extremely effective, it is clean, sharp with vivid, deep, rich color. Should have scored higher imo.', '2008-07-18 14:37:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832811, 696014, 30982, '<td valign="top">Love the glow!  Probably not what people were expecting for a "point" in the strictest of terms.  Was the light coming solely from above, or also lit from behind?</td>', 'Love the glow!  Probably not what people were expecting for a "point" in the strictest of terms.  Was the light coming solely from above, or also lit from behind?', '2008-07-18 18:05:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832814, 696094, 30982, '<td valign="top">How cool that it''s actually growing there.  I thought it had been placed.  Very much meets the challenge, and I like the contrast of the gravel to the very determined flower of considerably different and softer texture.</td>', 'How cool that it''s actually growing there.  I thought it had been placed.  Very much meets the challenge, and I like the contrast of the gravel to the very determined flower of considerably different and softer texture.', '2008-07-18 18:06:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832817, 694918, 30982, '<td valign="top">I love the smile in this!  It''s very genuine, very warm.  I think it meets the challenge, but I think the technicals hurt your score - on my monitor it''s very grainy.  And for DPC, it''s probably not nearly "set up" enough.  :-)</td>', 'I love the smile in this!  It''s very genuine, very warm.  I think it meets the challenge, but I think the technicals hurt your score - on my monitor it''s very grainy.  And for DPC, it''s probably not nearly "set up" enough.  :-)', '2008-07-18 18:08:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832818, 696144, 30982, '<td valign="top">The thing I like about this one is the green glow at the rim of his hat from the bokeh.  It''s a very nicely done portrait - great exposure to get the detail in the shirt - I find red is tough to get right!</td>', 'The thing I like about this one is the green glow at the rim of his hat from the bokeh.  It''s a very nicely done portrait - great exposure to get the detail in the shirt - I find red is tough to get right!', '2008-07-18 18:09:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832822, 695754, 30982, '<td valign="top">Definitely points in color at any rate!  Wonderful DOF here and the composition is perfect.  Great job of getting rich warm color without resorting to HSL, too.</td>', 'Definitely points in color at any rate!  Wonderful DOF here and the composition is perfect.  Great job of getting rich warm color without resorting to HSL, too.', '2008-07-18 18:11:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832824, 695591, 30982, '<td valign="top">This was one of my highest rated shots in the challenge.  Great find, fits the challenge perfectly in my opinion!</td>', 'This was one of my highest rated shots in the challenge.  Great find, fits the challenge perfectly in my opinion!', '2008-07-18 18:12:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832826, 695419, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like how you caught both the one going off and the trails of the one before it.  Probably not enough "color" to please some, but sure seems to have met the challenge!</td>', 'I like how you caught both the one going off and the trails of the one before it.  Probably not enough "color" to please some, but sure seems to have met the challenge!', '2008-07-18 18:13:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832829, 695410, 30982, '<td valign="top">Ah ha!  I was wondering where the ghost meter came from.  For the life of me, I couldn''t figure it out.  And it''s the most interesting and bizarre lens flare I''ve ever seen.  (Mine always seems to be just big green globs.)  Sure it wasn''t an alien??</td>', 'Ah ha!  I was wondering where the ghost meter came from.  For the life of me, I couldn''t figure it out.  And it''s the most interesting and bizarre lens flare I''ve ever seen.  (Mine always seems to be just big green globs.)  Sure it wasn''t an alien??', '2008-07-18 18:15:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832831, 696066, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done shot - well exposed, good choice of DOF.  The part I like best is that little star bud below the flower.  For some reason I keep going back to that.</td>', 'Very nicely done shot - well exposed, good choice of DOF.  The part I like best is that little star bud below the flower.  For some reason I keep going back to that.', '2008-07-18 18:17:24.000000', NULL, 0),
